# service-wifi's R8 classpath holds framework-wifi twice, before and after jarjar, and which
# copy of an AIDL interface R8 resolves varies from run to run. Taking the pre-jarjar one, the
# binder methods whose signatures name a jarjared type (ParceledListSlice) look like they
# override nothing and are shrunk away, and system_server dies on the first call to one.
-keepclassmembers class * implements android.os.IInterface {
    public <methods>;
}
